// The board games lab: the debug world set's game station on one small floor under a clear day, booted alone so a change
// to a board game, its pieces, its cards, its seats or the station's holodeck bakes and settles in a fraction of the debug
// world's time. Boot it with `--world worlds/debug/labs/board-games.puck`; the seat starts at the station's near chair
// (`hero`), a second seat at its far chair (`rival`), and the context button sits a seat down at the glass.
//
// What it holds, and nothing else:
//
//   - one game station (../game-stations.puck over ../../standard/game-station.puck) at the origin, showing chess,
//     Klondike and FreeCell from its menu. Its board is a holodeck: chess stands its 32 pieces on the glass as rigid
//     bodies a seated player lifts and sets down (or anyone knocks over), and the settled board is judged; Klondike and
//     FreeCell stand their 52 cards and deal from the station's own seeded stream once shown. Switching games releases
//     one game's bodies and stands the other's. game-station.md says how to play and drive it;
//   - a floor, a sun and the Moth to walk it.
//
// The Go and Reversi tables are not here. ../go.puck and ../reversi.puck are whole documents of the gallery's board game
// room, not modules: each imports the gallery's whole shape catalog (../shapes.puck), derives its body slots from
// the gallery's population and the other tables' counts (`galleryPopulation`, `boardRoomBodies`, `alchemyBodies`),
// grants the seat Drive over bodies by those absolute indices, and stands at the gallery's level-2 coordinates. Standing
// either here would stand the gallery beside it until they become stations' games.
//
// The portal hook is the id `board-games`. The gallery's lab wing connects it with one painting row named `board-games`
// whose destination is the reference `board-games` (this document), and a crossing arrives at the spawn point
// `board-games`, beside the station and facing it.
//
// `board-games-stress.puck` beside this file is twelve stations, each playing chess against itself.

schema: "puck.world.definition.v1"
basis: "../avatars/moth"
documentId: "board-games"

import "../set-controls"
import "../../standard/skies"
import "../../standard/inputs"
import "../game-stations"

metadata {
  title: "Board games lab"
  description: "A game station showing chess, Klondike and FreeCell as holodeck bodies, on a small floor."
}

gameStationRoom(stations: [rootStation])

// The hook's arrival, beside the station's near chair and facing the glass.
spawnPoints [
  { id: "board-games", position [-2, 0, -3], yawDegrees: 180 }
]

state {
  // The chess game's vocabularies (../game-stations.puck's header).
  enum PieceKind {
    None
    Pawn
    Knight
    Bishop
    Rook
    Queen
    King
  }

  enum MoveKind {
    Illegal
    Quiet
    Capture
    EnPassant
    Castle
  }

  enum TurnColor {
    White
    Black
  }
}

use gameStationGames as station(station: rootStation, index: 0)

render {
  farDistance: 200
  lighting {
    lights [
      sunlight(direction: [-2, 4, -3], color: "#FFF1D6", illuminance: 60000lx)
    ]
  }
  sky {
    clearDay()
  }
  atmosphere {
    clearDayAir()
  }
}
